      "id": "s1",
      "template": "title",
      "narration": "ChatGPT doesn't read text the way you think! It processes text using something called tokens.",
      "text": {
        "heading": "What Are Tokens?",
        "sub": "The building blocks of AI text"
      },
      "durationSec": 7.128
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "template": "code",
      "narration": "Look at this sentence: I love coding. An AI tokenizer splits text into smaller pieces called tokens.",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Step 1: Split the Text",
        "code": [
          "Input:",
          "\"I love coding!\"",
          "",
          "Tokens:",
          "[\"I\", \" love\",",
          " \" coding\", \"!\"]",
          "",
          "# Illustrative token split"
        ]
      },
      "durationSec": 7.56
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "template": "code",
      "narration": "A token can be a whole word, part of a word, or even punctuation. Different models may split the same text differently.",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Step 2: What Counts?",
        "code": [
          "Whole word: \"AI\"",
          "",
          "Word parts:",
          "\"un\" + \"believ\" + \"able\"",
          "",
          "Punctuation: \"!\"",
          "",
          "# Examples only"
        ]
      },
      "durationSec": 8.424
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "template": "code",
      "narration": "Why do tokens matter? Your prompt and the model's response use tokens. They affect context limits and often determine API usage costs.",
      "text": {
        "heading": "Step 3: Why Tokens Matter",
        "code": [
          "Your Prompt",
          "     ↓",
          "Input Tokens",
          "     ↓",
          "AI Model",
          "     ↓",
          "Output Tokens",
          "",
          "# Context + API Cost"
        ]
      },
      "durationSec": 10.392
